    "description": "Infinite is a PHP constant, called ``INF``. It is also possible to generate such a value, with calls to math functions such as ``log(0)`` or ``1e308 * 2``.\n\nWhile the infinite is a float, it is possible to test a number with ``is_infinite()``.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n$infinite = 1e308 * 2;\n\nvar_dump(is_infinite($infinite)); // true \n\nvar_dump(INF === $infinite);      // true \n\necho str_repeat('1', 1000) + 0;  // INF\n\n?>",
